ZeroTwo Launcher — Development Plan

Project

An Android launcher for Minecraft Java Edition, based on Zalith Launcher.

Design

- Dark black and plum interface
- Crimson and neon-pink accents
- Zero Two-inspired artwork
- Landscape-first layout
- Custom navigation and launcher dashboard

Accounts

- Microsoft account login
- Offline profiles
- Multiple local profiles

Minecraft

- Version support targeting 26.2 and 26.3
- Support for older versions where compatible
- Java runtime management
- Per-version settings

Mod Hub

- Sodium and Sodium Extra
- Lithium and FerriteCore
- ImmediatelyFast and Entity Culling
- Compatibility and dependency checks
- Performance presets

Other Features

- Modpack manager
- Download manager
- Touch-control editor
- Crash log analyzer
- World backups
- Resource-pack manager
- Skin studio
- Screenshot gallery
- Performance overlay
- Custom Minecraft main menu and pause menu

Restrictions

- No shaders or shader manager.
- Preserve existing Zalith Launcher functionality.
- Respect mod licenses and download sources.

Status

Planning and source integration in progress. Features are not yet implemented or tested.